  "body": "One is #event-{input,change}, with the dfn being in the appendix, which is used for select and textarea. The other is #event-input-{input,change}, with the dfn being in the middle of the form controls area.\n\nIt seems like the appendix only contains rows for the select/textarea ones, with \"see also\" in the description column referring to the others.\n\nAlso there seems to be a typo: the second \"Fired at controls when the user changes the value (see also the change event of input elements)\" should probably say \"input event\".\n\nThis is confusing. I think the best fix would be to use the same events for input elements, textareas, and selects, and update the appendix to be more clear about the different types of targets.\n",
